{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS4cb5NHABbPcsHUy8qt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bug is fixed. The cause was that each publish stores a similarity score for the related stories, and that score was a Python `float`, which DynamoDB rejects. The first publish worked only because the table was empty, so there were no related stories and no scores to store. From the second publish on, saving the story fails with `TypeError: Float types are not supported`, and the handler turns that into a 500.\n\n**Fix, in `src/app.py`:**\n- `similarity()` now returns the score as a `Decimal`, which DynamoDB accepts, instead of a `float`.\n- **So it can't come back:** a new `to_dynamo()` helper converts any `float` anywhere in a story to a `Decimal` right before it's saved. A float field added later will be converted instead of causing another 500.\n\n**Tests, in `tests/test_publish.py`:**\n- One new test publishes three stories in a row, which is the case that failed in production. On the old code it fails with the same 500.\n- A second test checks the new helper.\n\nAll 3 tests pass with the fix.\n\nI also noticed that `publish()` reads only the first page of results when it looks up existing stories. Once the table grows past 1 MB, related stories will be picked from only part of the library. It isn't related to the 500, so I mentioned it in `ANSWER.md` but didn't change it.\n\nThe changes aren't committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":985,"cache_read_input_tokens":26015,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":985},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f52f2fe2-f6a7-47a4-8f70-42c10f7e8a7c","uuid":"815dd0d5-eb52-4c34-b692-fd17a896f791","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:52:12.388Z","request_id":"req_011CgS4carEBz7XfySK7jw6S"}
